**user**:
> How can I make a string in c++ that looks like "file-" + number + ".csv"?
**assistant**:
> In C++, you can build that string a few common ways.
> 
> If you’re using modern C++ (C++11 or later):
> 
> ```cpp
> #include <string>
> 
> int number = 42;
> std::string filename = "file-" + std::to_string(number) + ".csv";
> ```
> 
> That’s the simplest.
> 
> If you prefer using streams:
> 
> ```cpp
> #include <sstream>
> #include <string>
> 
> int number = 42;
> std::ostringstream oss;
> oss << "file-" << number << ".csv";
> std::string filename = oss.str();
> ```
> 
> Or in C++20 with `std::format`:
> 
> ```cpp
> #include <format>
> #include <string>
> 
> int number = 42;
> std::string filename = std::format("file-{}.csv", number);
> ```
> 
> Use whichever matches the C++ standard your compiler supports.
